  "prefLabel": "Nat 701.01 Definitions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Nat 701.01 Definitions.\n\n(a) “Substantially identical molecular structure of synthetically produced substances” means a substance with a related or fundamental aspect to a naturally occurring substance in plants, animals or humans in terms of mechanism of action or pharmacology.\n\nSource. #13140, eff 11-26-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/nat100-700.html"
